{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And let my name be called upon them, and the name of my fathers.</b> That there be called upon them all that my name and the name of my fathers indicate — for the name יִשְׂרָאֵל is on account of ״כִּי שָׂרִיתָ עִם אֱלֹהִים וַאֲנָשִׁים״ (Genesis 32:29) — so shall a righteous person rule in the fear of HaShem; and יַעֲקֹב is on account of עֵקֶב, the great abundance of good hidden away for the righteous, for their beginning is always small but their end increases greatly; and אַבְרָהָם is on account of ״אַב הֲמוֹן גּוֹיִם״ (Genesis 17:5) — so shall they be the head of all the nations; and יִצְחָק, its translation is וַחֲדִי (rejoice) — so shall joy always be in their dwelling." "<b>And may they swarm into a multitude in the midst of the earth.</b> He should have said בָּאָרֶץ — what is בְּקֶרֶב הָאָרֶץ? And it appears that one may explain it along the lines of what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sotah 11a): that the Egyptians would plow over them and a miracle was done for them and they were swallowed into the ground, etc., and afterward they would emerge and bubble up and go home in flocks, etc. And according to this, they were indeed fruitful and multiplied בְּקֶרֶב הָאָרֶץ, literally — for not for nothing was this miracle done for them, that they were swallowed into the ground, but surely so that the evil eye of the Egyptians should not have dominion over them. Therefore they were covered over in the earth like fish that are covered in the water, and by virtue of their being literally בְּקֶרֶב הָאָרֶץ, they became many like fish — for the evil eye did not have dominion over them. And of this it is said: ״וַתִּמָּלֵא הָאָרֶץ אֹתָם״ (Exodus 1:7)." "And He gave the blessing of multiplicity specifically to Joseph, for his name indicates increase and multiplication, as it is written (Genesis 30:24) ״יוֹסֵף ה׳ לִי בֵּן אַחֵר״, and as it is written (Deuteronomy 1:11) ״יוֹסֵף עֲלֵיכֶם כָּכֶם אֶלֶף פְּעָמִים״. And this blessing was especially fitting for Ephraim, on account of ״כִּי הִפְרַנִי אֱלֹהִים״; therefore he placed his right hand on the head of Ephraim, for Jacob thought that his name would assist him in receiving this blessing. And Joseph thought that it was more fitting to attach the blessing of multiplicity to the firstborn, for to him belongs a double portion in the inheritance; therefore the blessing of multiplicity too suited him more. And Jacob answered: ״יָדַעְתִּי בְנִי יָדַעְתִּי״. He mentioned ״יָדַעְתִּי״ twice, corresponding to the double-portion blessing of the firstborn. And he said ״גַּם הוּא יִגְדָּל וְגַם הוּא יִהְיֶה לְעָם״ — he mentioned two ״גַּם״s, to hint at the doubling, as if to say: I know from the double portion of the firstborn — for from this side it would have been proper to give him the greater share in the blessing of multiplicity, to join both considerations together — but nevertheless ״אָחִיו הַקָּטֹן יִגְדַּל מִמֶּנּוּ״, for the Holy One, blessed be He, chooses the smaller ones to a greater degree. And any person in whom there is an aspect of smallness — then the Holy One, blessed be He, elevates him all the more, to set him for thousands and ten thousands, as it is written (Deuteronomy 7:7) ״לֹא מֵרֻבְּכֶם מִכָּל הָעַמִּים חָשַׁק ה׳ בָּכֶם וגו׳ כִּי אַתֶּם הַמְעַט״, and it is written (Isaiah 60:22) ״הַקָּטֹן יִהְיֶה לְאֶלֶף וְהַצָּעִיר לְגוֹי עָצוּם״. And this happened to all the seed of Abraham: Ishmael was firstborn to Abraham — Ishmael was rejected and Isaac was chosen; Esau was firstborn to Isaac — Esau was rejected and Jacob was chosen; Reuben was firstborn to Jacob — Reuben was rejected and Joseph was chosen; Manasseh was firstborn to Joseph — Ephraim was chosen to a greater degree. And this hint — is it not a thing? And those who understand will comprehend."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:23.073782860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}